BEGIN_DESC
Near the Sun, 0.278 AU (41.57 million km, 59.8 solar radii): the critical mark of the light suit.
Kaira Rean (Karkas, Suit_T10, set Boron: sunlight absorptance 0.22) is at its rated limit here: the suit's surroundings
are +121 C (the radiative balance in full sunlight, 17.6 kW/m2 = 12.9 Suns). Any closer and the environment is out of
the suit's limits.
Niza Krit (Pantsir, Suit_T30, rated to +430 C) has margin: her own critical mark lies at 0.083 AU (17.9 solar radii).
The Delta-glider GL-01 is a few metres away, all three on a circular orbit round the Sun.
